Isaac Sim benchmark

- vlmpilot/src/vlmpilot/controller/isaacsim/pegasus_*.py, verifier/isaacsim/, vlmpilot/configs/isaacsim/single-drone/ and scripts/isaacsim/ drive Isaac Sim (https://developer.nvidia.com/isaac/sim) through Pegasus Simulator (https://github.com/PegasusSimulator/PegasusSimulator, BSD-3-Clause) and PX4-Autopilot (https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot, BSD-3-Clause), talking to PX4 through MAVSDK-Python (https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK-Python, BSD-3-Clause). They are installed from their upstream sources by scripts/runpod/isaacsim/setup.sh.
- scripts/isaacsim/pegasus_sim.py is based on examples/1_px4_single_vehicle.py of Pegasus Simulator (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2023, Marcelo Fialho Jacinto; full license text below). No other Pegasus, PX4 or MAVSDK code is included.
- vlmpilot/src/vlmpilot/controller/isaacsim/pegasus_link.py has no counterpart in the Pegasus examples and was written from scratch against the MAVSDK API.
- Isaac Sim and its assets (Brownstone demo pack, vMaterials, Isaac people characters) are NVIDIA software under the NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Omniverse license. They are not redistributed; setup downloads them from NVIDIA's public servers after you accept the license.
- The car target is CarConcept by Eric Chadwick / Darmstadt Graphics Group GmbH (2024), from the Khronos glTF-Sample-Assets, licensed CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Setup downloads it and converts it to USD.

